# Security response headers, served by Cloudflare Workers Static Assets (it honors _headers).
# Addresses the (unscored) Lighthouse security recommendations: a Content Security Policy,
# a strong HSTS policy (with preload), and clickjacking / MIME protections.
#
# CSP notes for maintainers:
#   - script-src is tight: 'self' + the inline anti-FOUC theme script ('unsafe-inline',
#     unavoidable on a static build with no per-request nonce) + the Cloudflare Web
#     Analytics beacon. It still blocks externally-loaded scripts.
#   - img-src / media-src allow https: so Sanity images (cdn.sanity.io) and editor-added
#     images / background videos load.
#   - frame-src lists the embeds actually used (YouTube, Vimeo, Google Maps). If a church
#     later adds a Subsplash / Planning Center script or iframe embed via the page builder,
#     add its origin to script-src / frame-src.
#   - connect-src: the Sanity-built forms post to this site's own /api/contact/ ('self',
#     starter card 45, 2026-10-13). https://api.web3forms.com stays ONLY for the
#     newsletter signup's fallback (src/lib/subscribe.ts) and can go once that has an ESP
#     form URL in Studio; form-action keeps it for the same reason.
#   - Cloudflare Turnstile (form anti-spam, replaced hCaptcha 2026-10-13) needs
#     https://challenges.cloudflare.com in script-src (api.js) and frame-src (the widget
#     iframe). Its own requests run inside that iframe, so connect-src needs nothing. The
#     token is verified server-side by the Worker. Without these two the widget is
#     silently blocked and never appears. NOTE: a plain local static preview does NOT
#     send these headers, so always check the widget against `wrangler dev` or the live
#     site, not just a static file server.
#   - frame-ancestors is 'self': the Presentation preview iframes /preview/* from the
#     EMBEDDED same-origin /studio, so 'self' is exactly right.
#   - The embedded Sanity Studio (/studio) needs: Sanity API + websocket origins in
#     connect-src, Google Fonts (Fraunces/Source Sans studio chrome) in style-src +
#     font-src, design-system-static.sanity.io in font-src (the Studio's own Inter
#     webfont -- blocked fonts showed up as console CSP errors on the first deploy),
#     sanity-cdn.com in connect-src (the Studio's module/version check pings it;
#     blocked showed as 'Failed to fetch version for package' console errors),
#     and blob: workers in worker-src.
#   - Trusted Types is intentionally NOT enabled: require-trusted-types-for would break the
#     YouTube / Vimeo / Maps / analytics / embed scripts.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'self'; img-src 'self' data: https:; media-src 'self' https:; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com https://design-system-static.sanity.io; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com https://www.googletagmanager.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com; connect-src 'self' https://api.web3forms.com https://cloudflareinsights.com https://www.googletagmanager.com https://www.google-analytics.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://stats.g.doubleclick.net https://api.sanity.io https://*.api.sanity.io wss://*.api.sanity.io https://*.apicdn.sanity.io https://sanity-cdn.com https://*.sanity-cdn.com; frame-src 'self' https://www.youtube.com https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com https://www.google.com https://maps.google.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com; form-action 'self' https://api.web3forms.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; upgrade-insecure-requests
